    ],
    "name": "Latin AltGr demo (example)",
    "version": "0.1.0",
    "license": "MIT-0",
    "description": "Example (b): QWERTY letters and digits (the punctuation positions are in the form but unbound) with an AltGr layer, dead keys, a chained dead key on AltGr+6 to AltGr+0 (circumflex then dot below, or the reverse, gives a third dead key), a dead key with noMatch emitText, multi-unit outputs (AltGr+Q gives a + combining acute; AltGr+M a supplementary character) and a multi-unit dead-key result (diaeresis then AltGr+Q gives ä + combining acute, compiled for Windows by the multi-unit recipe). Normalisation is disabled (settings.normalization, D75): the multi-unit recipe works on exact code points, and NFC would turn a + combining acute into one character.",
    "authors": [
      {
        "name": "The YAKBD contributors"
      }
    ]
  },
